{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:22:48.744Z","data":{"turn":12,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01GtnUbab9y329X7RgUmExU3\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Architecture Scanner Agent\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security-focused architecture analyst. Analyze this codebase thoroughly and provide a comprehensive security-relevant architectural summary.\\n\\n**Tasks:**\\n1. Identify the complete technology stack (languages, frameworks, databases, servers)\\n2. Read package.json, docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile, knexfile.js, and any config files\\n3. Explore the src/ directory structure and identify all modules\\n4. Explore the client/ directory to understand the frontend\\n5. Read nginx configuration files\\n6. Identify architectural patterns (MVC, microservices, monolith, etc.)\\n7. Map trust boundaries between components\\n8. Identify security-relevant configurations and their implications\\n9. Check .env.example for environment variables and security settings\\n10. Look at the migrations/ and seeds/ directories for database schema info\\n\\n**Output Format:** Provide a detailed report covering:\\n- Complete tech stack with versions where available\\n- Architectural pattern and component relationships\\n- Trust boundaries (frontend ↔ API ↔ database ↔ external services)\\n- Security-relevant configuration findings\\n- Database technologies and how they're used\\n- External service integrations\\n- Deployment architecture (Docker, nginx config)\\n- Any security misconfigurations or concerns found\\n\\nBe thorough - read actual file contents, not just filenames. Focus on security implications of every finding.\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:22:48.744Z"}}
