{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:22:55.122Z","data":{"turn":14,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01EMahoDw8UEUoZWt6DxfTEJ\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"find /repos/webvulnbench -maxdepth 2 -type f -name \\\"*.json\\\" -o -name \\\"*.yml\\\" -o -name \\\"*.yaml\\\" -o -name \\\"Dockerfile*\\\" -o -name \\\".env*\\\" -o -name \\\"*.conf\\\" -o -name \\\"knexfile*\\\" | sort\",\"description\":\"Find config files\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:22:55.122Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:22:55.274Z","data":{"turn":15,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01DjKrYZijrPrm3MGepg62gL\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Entry Point Mapper Agent\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security analyst specializing in attack surface mapping. Find ALL network-accessible entry points in this Node.js application.\\n\\n**Tasks:**\\n1. Search for ALL Express route definitions across the entire src/ directory. Look for patterns like:\\n   - router.get, router.post, router.put, router.patch, router.delete\\n   - app.get, app.post, app.put, app.patch, app.delete\\n   - app.use (for middleware mounting)\\n2. Find the main application entry point (likely src/index.js or src/app.js) and trace how routes are mounted\\n3. Read EVERY route file in src/ subdirectories to catalog every endpoint\\n4. Identify which endpoints are public vs authenticated\\n5. Find any file upload endpoints\\n6. Find any webhook or callback endpoints\\n7. Look for API schema files (OpenAPI/Swagger JSON/YAML, GraphQL schemas)\\n8. Check for WebSocket endpoints\\n9. Look for any admin endpoints or debug routes\\n10. Check client/src/ for API call patterns to discover endpoints from the consumer side\\n\\n**Output Format:** Provide a complete catalog of ALL endpoints with:\\n- HTTP method and path\\n- Which file defines it\\n- Whether it requires authentication\\n- What input it accepts (body, query params, file uploads)\\n- Security relevance (file upload, admin, payment, etc.)\\n- Any middleware applied to the route\\n\\nGroup endpoints by module/domain (auth, users, gigs, payments, etc.). Be exhaustive - missing an endpoint means a blind spot in the security assessment.\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:22:55.274Z"}}
