{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:23:03.676Z","data":{"turn":32,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01VJ5jH7LddavdX5yhnfu6Xy\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Security Pattern Hunter Agent\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security architecture specialist. Identify ALL authentication, authorization, and security mechanisms in this Node.js application.\\n\\n**Tasks:**\\n1. Find and read ALL middleware files in src/middleware/\\n2. Find JWT implementation - token generation, validation, refresh, storage\\n3. Find password hashing implementation (bcrypt, argon2, etc.)\\n4. Find session management code\\n5. Find RBAC/permission checking code\\n6. Find CORS configuration\\n7. Find rate limiting implementation\\n8. Find input validation/sanitization code\\n9. Find security headers configuration (helmet, custom headers)\\n10. Find CSRF protection\\n11. Find OAuth/SSO/OIDC flows if present\\n12. Find file upload security (type checking, size limits, storage)\\n13. Search for cookie configuration (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite flags)\\n14. Find any API key authentication\\n15. Check nginx config for security headers (HSTS, CSP, etc.)\\n\\n**For each finding, provide:**\\n- Exact file path and relevant line numbers\\n- How the mechanism works\\n- Security strengths and weaknesses\\n- Potential bypass scenarios\\n- Missing security controls that should be present\\n\\n**Authentication endpoints to catalog:**\\n- Login, logout, register, password reset, token refresh, email verification\\n- Include exact routes and file locations\\n\\nBe thorough - read actual source code of every security-relevant file. This analysis determines whether the pentest team can find auth bypasses.\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:23:03.676Z"}}
