{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:26:10.394Z","data":{"turn":173,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01CCr36sW72FddkMsvj9ergF\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"XSS/Injection Sink Hunter\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security specialist focused on finding XSS and injection sinks. Analyze this Node.js freelance marketplace application (HireFlow/WebVulnBench).\\n\\n**CONTEXT:** This is a Node.js Express backend with a React (Vite) frontend in client/src/. The backend serves the React SPA. Key backend modules are in src/ with subdirectories: auth, users, gigs, contracts, payments, messaging, reviews, disputes, notifications, admin, integrations, middleware, utils, config, models.\\n\\n**Tasks:**\\n\\n### Backend (Server-Side Injection Sinks):\\n1. Read ALL service files in src/*/service.js or src/*/*.service.js - find:\\n   - SQL injection: raw SQL queries, string interpolation in queries, whereRaw, knex.raw\\n   - NoSQL injection: MongoDB $where, string-built queries, unsanitized operators\\n   - Command injection: exec, spawn, child_process usage\\n   - Template injection: any server-side template rendering with user data\\n   - Deserialization: JSON.parse of user input, eval(), Function(), vm.runInNewContext\\n2. Read src/utils/pdf.js - analyze HTML template generation for server-side XSS via Puppeteer\\n3. Read ALL controller files for unvalidated user input passed to services\\n4. Check for eval(), Function(), setTimeout/setInterval with string args\\n\\n### Frontend (Client-Side XSS Sinks):\\n5. Read ALL files in client/src/ - search for:\\n   - dangerouslySetInnerHTML usage in React components\\n   - innerHTML, outerHTML assignments\\n   - document.write, document.writeln\\n   - jQuery DOM manipulation (.html(), .append() with user data)\\n   - eval(), Function(), setTimeout with strings\\n   - URL manipulation (location.href, window.open with user data)\\n   - DOM-based XSS via URL params (useSearchParams, window.location)\\n6. Check for any unescaped rendering of user-provided content (reviews, messages, gig descriptions, profile data)\\n\\n**Output Format:** For EACH sink found, provide:\\n- Exact file path with line numbers\\n- The vulnerable code snippet\\n- The render context (HTML body, attribute, JavaScript, URL, CSS)\\n- Whether it's network-reachable (can be triggered by a request)\\n- Severity assessment\\n- Attack scenario\\n\\nBe exhaustive. Check every file in client/src/ and every service/controller in src/.\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:26:10.394Z"}}
